          "%md",
          "",
          "### Step 6: Structural Ranking",
          "",
          "Rank all Step 3b candidates, so the review in Step 5 starts in a defensible order. The query combines two measures:",
          "",
          "- `candidate_user_fan_in`: how many candidate accounts share the same computer. A computer that only one or two accounts use persistently looks like a targeted relationship. A computer that hundreds of accounts use looks like shared infrastructure.",
          "- `pagerank_score`: how central the computer is in the cyber graph, computed with `DBMS_OGA.PAGERANK`. A central computer, such as a domain controller or a jump host, turns a hit into a statement about business impact.",
          "",
          "The result lists the confirmed pairs first, then the candidates with the lowest fan-in, and within the same fan-in the highest PageRank. Fan-in comes first because PageRank alone favors shared infrastructure, such as domain controllers and file servers, that many accounts use. The computers of the three confirmed pairs score between 1.1e-5 and 7.4e-5, while the highest-ranked unlabeled candidate, `C1973`, scores 7.7e-4. Use the top rows as input for Step 5.",
          "",
          "Step 6a computes the PageRank scores once and stores them. Step 6b ranks the candidates."
        ],
