        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "**6a.** Compute PageRank for every computer in the cyber graph and store the scores in the table `computer_pagerank`. Graph algorithm results exist only while the query that computes them runs. The table keeps the scores, so the ranking query and any repeated run do not compute them again. All three scenarios use the same scores: Scenarios 1 and 2 keep the table, and the Clean Up step of Scenario 3 drops it.",
          "",
          "> **Note:** PageRank on the full cyber graph is expensive, and this statement can run for about 18 minutes. If the table already exists, for example from a previous scenario, the statement leaves it as it is and returns at once."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
